WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.620
Over the course of five seasons, Breaking
Bad told the tale of Walter White, a man whose

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.680
cancer diagnosis drove him to cook and sell
meth.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.960
Now, we’re going to dig deep and explain
the story of the timid chemistry teacher who

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.140
finally broke bad.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:21.160
In the first episode of Breaking Bad, high
school chemistry teacher Walter White is diagnosed

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.500
with terminal lung cancer.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:28.160
After finding out from Hank Schrader, his
DEA agent brother-in-law, how profitable cooking

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:33.949
meth can be, Walt teams up with a former student
named Jesse Pinkman to cook meth so that he

00:00:33.949 --> 00:00:37.120
can make enough money to provide for his family
after he's gone.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:42.500
Unfortunately, Jesse and their batch of newly
cooked meth are snatched up by a pair of dealers

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.400
named Krazy-8 and Emilio.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.499
The two force Jesse to take them to the RV
where Walt and Jesse have been cooking, presumably

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.640
to kill the two and to take their materials.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:56.839
Walt poisons the two of them, but Krazy-8
survives long enough that Walt is forced to

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.580
kill the meth dealer himself.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:04.100
Soon after, Walt's family pushes him to pursue
chemotherapy rather than just accept his fate.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.520
Ultimately, Walt agrees to seek treatment,
even though the cost would put his family

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.680
even further into debt.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.060
Walt and Jesse make their partnership official
with a simple division of labor: Walt will

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.380
cook, while Jesse will sell.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.420
"The chemistry is my realm.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.840
I am in charge of the cooking.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.440
Out there on the street, you deal with that."

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:29.980
Jesse reaches out to a local crime boss, Tuco
Salamanca, to see if he'd be interested in

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.200
buying larger quantities of the pair's high-quality
meth.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.980
To put it simply, negotiations do not go well.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:41.710
Walt moves in to handle Tuco, using his chemistry
skills to prepare an explosion to intimidate

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:42.200
Tuco.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.260
Impressed and amused, Tuco agrees to work
with Walt and Jesse.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.710
The two make a deal with Tuco that they'll
make meth for him to sell, while he pays them

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.360
enough to make it worth their while.

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:57.240
To keep his identity a secret, Walt adopts
the persona of "Heisenberg," and it seems

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.960
like Walter will be able to keep his "second
job" a secret from his family.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:07.720
Unfortunately, Tuco is about as stable as
a meth kingpin can be when said kingpin also

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.220
indulges in his own product.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:14.580
After a paranoid fit in which he believes
that the DEA is closing in on him, Tuco kidnaps

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:18.060
Walt and Jesse to force them to continue cooking
meth for him.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.800
While being held hostage, Walt and Jesse nearly
manage to poison Tuco with ricin, but Tuco's

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.660
mute, wheelchair-bound uncle, Hector, alerts
him to their plan.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.720
Luckily, they're saved when Hank stumbles
onto Tuco and shoots him dead during a shootout.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:37.360
Having barely survived their run-in with the
real criminal underworld, Jesse and Walt try

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.360
to take a break from the meth business.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:44.260
Jesse shacks up with a friend of his to provide
an alibi when the cops come looking for him,

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.180
while Walt feigns stress-induced amnesia to
explain his extended disappearance.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.420
Walt tries to reconnect with his family when
they become worried about his health after

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:58.840
his "fugue state," but that only brings up
more underlying issues with his pregnant wife,

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.340
Skyler.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:04.680
Meanwhile, Jesse finds himself kicked out
of his aunt's house and out of friends after

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.520
the double whammy of being kidnapped and drawing
the interest of the DEA.

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:13.440
On the other side of the law, Hank's killing
of Tuco leads to a sizable promotion for him,

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.780
but it also causes a heaping amount of stress
and anxiety after the shootout.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.980
Walt and Jesse try to establish themselves
as serious contenders in the power vacuum

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:28.340
created by Tuco's death, operating as cooks
and distributors within Tuco's former territory.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.159
A series of accidents leaves Jesse with a
reputation as a cold-blooded killer, which

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.800
seems to establish "Heisenberg" as a genuine
power player.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.080
On the home front, things have gotten complicated.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.920
As a cover for all his meth money, Walt has
been telling Skyler that his former business

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:47.060
partners, Gretchen and Elliott, have been
paying for his cancer treatments.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:51.100
But when Gretchen finds out about the lie,
she tells Skyler than she won't be paying

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.700
for any more therapy, leaving Walt to search
for another cover story.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.400
"We'll get through this, okay?

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:04.160
I mean, they've already paid for most of my
treatment, right?"

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:09.700
On top of all that, Walt and Jesse end up
attracting attention from the law after Badger,

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.600
one of their meth dealers, is arrested.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:17.020
With the help of Saul Goodman, a local criminal
lawyer, they devise a plan to trick the DEA

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:21.900
into arresting a fake "Heisenberg," freeing
Badger and taking the heat off Walt.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:26.180
The plan goes smoothly, although Hank remains
convinced that something is wrong.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.240
Everything seems to be going to plan.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:33.620
Walt is making money, and Jesse's ongoing
romance with his neighbor and landlord, Jane,

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:38.000
continues even when she realizes that he's
a drug dealer, and he realizes that she's

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.420
in recovery for addiction.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.140
After one of Jesse's drug dealer friends is
killed by a rival gang, Jesse and Walt realize

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.860
they aren't cut out to manage a crew of drug
dealers.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.580
So with Saul's help, Walt and Jesse find a
distributor for their surplus meth.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:58.300
The mysterious buyer, Gus Fring, is a fast
food franchise owner and model citizen who

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:03.900
uses his role as the public face of Los Pollos
Hermanos to disguise his illicit activities.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:08.840
Those high expectations extend to his employees,
and when Jesse shows up to a meeting high,

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:12.060
Gus doesn't think that Jesse is competent
enough to handle the work.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.760
It turns out he might have been right.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:18.520
When Walt gets notice that Gus needs their
drugs on short notice, he finds that Jesse

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:22.980
is completely incapacitated from his drug
use and unable to make the drop.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:27.960
Unfortunately, Walt is also needed at the
hospital, where Skyler is in labor, delivering

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.460
their daughter.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:34.000
Walt ultimately chooses to make the delivery,
missing the birth of his child, but he nets

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.920
over $1 million for him and Jesse to split.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:41.400
However, Walt refuses to pay Jesse his share
until he gets clean.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:47.430
Desperate for cash after her father nearly
takes her to rehab, Jane blackmails Walt into

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.080
giving them the money immediately.

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:53.620
Walt does, but finds himself coming back to
check on Jesse and try to get him help.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.780
While shaking a sleeping Jesse, Walt accidentally
knocks an unconscious Jane onto her back,

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:03.240
and when she starts to choke on her own vomit,
he watches her die without interfering.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:09.400
Weeks later, incapacitated by grief, Jane's
father, an air traffic controller, lets two

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.060
planes collide over the skies of Albuquerque.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:18.200
After the plane crash, Jesse lands in rehab,
blaming himself for Jane's death and everything

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:22.630
else, while Skyler's taken the kids and moved
out, leaving Walt to contemplate what he's

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:23.780
still working towards.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:29.000
Skyler finds out the truth that Walt is a
meth cook and offers him an ultimatum; agree

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.860
to a divorce, or she'll tell Hank.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.780
"Nobody will hear it from me.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:37.460
But only if you grant me this divorce and
stay out of our lives."

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:42.460
Things get even more complicated when Gus
shows up with a new offer: $3 million for

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.080
three months work in a state-of-the art laboratory.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:50.160
Walt refuses in the moment, but trouble is
arriving from Mexico in the form of bloodthirsty

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.120
twins looking to enact vengeance on Heisenberg.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:57.940
Walt's attempts to get out of the drug business
aren't exactly helped along by anyone.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:03.120
Saul wants him to go back to cooking, while
Skyler is horrified by what he's already done.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:09.060
Unbeknownst to Walt, Gus strikes a deal with
the twins, who are Tuco Salamanca's cousins,

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:12.720
out for revenge, to keep Walt alive for Gus'
own purposes.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:18.300
Meanwhile, Jesse makes his own batch of meth,
offering to sell it to Gus against Walt's

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:18.800
wishes.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:23.460
Gus accepts the deal, knowing that Walt's
pride will bring him back to the meth cooking

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.580
business, a prediction that's ultimately proven
right.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:31.180
Walt accepts Gus' offer and pushes Jesse out
of the business, while Hank finds clues that

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.620
are starting to lead him to Jesse.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:37.720
Walt's feeling like a new man with his own
condo and a hidden laboratory for cooking

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:38.220
meth.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:43.260
Even better, he's got a new, eager-to-please
lab assistant, Gale Boetticher, who seems

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.520
like a serious upgrade compared to Jesse.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:50.920
Unfortunately, Walt's brought back into Jesse's
orbit when Hank accidentally warns Walt that

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.740
he's closing in on their old RV.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:57.860
Walt and Jesse manage to distract Hank with
a phony phone call alleging that his wife,

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.540
Marie, is in the hospital.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:04.720
Things get even worse for Hank when Gus, forced
to bargain with the twins, offers them Hank's

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:09.890
life instead of Heisenberg's, on the basis
that Hank is the one who actually killed their

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:10.760
cousin, Tuco.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:16.060
Believing Jesse to be behind the fake phone
call, Hank attacks Jesse, savagely beating

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:16.560
him.

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:21.860
After Jesse threatens to use the illegal beating
to make Hank's life miserable, Walt tries

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:26.990
to placate Jesse, offering him a job in the
meth lab. Jesse accepts the deal, which means

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:28.480
Walt has to fire Gale.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:33.460
The Salamanca twins attack Hank, but the DEA
agent kills one and puts the other in the

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.660
hospital, although he's wounded himself.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:40.240
Walt and Jesse resume their cooking for Gus,
although Jesse begins to take some of the

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.720
excess product in order to sell it on the
side.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:47.600
With Walt making plenty of money and Hank's
hospital bills stacking up, Skyler offers

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:52.720
to pay for his recovery, with the cover story
that Walt's meth money is actually earnings

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:53.820
from a gambling habit.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:57.060
But things never run smoothly for long in
Breaking Bad.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:01.920
After getting involved with Andrea, a woman
at his Narcotics Anonymous meetings, Jesse

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:07.180
is horrified to discover that the drug dealers
who killed his friend last season are also

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:09.740
using Andrea's 11-year-old brother to sell
meth.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:16.020
Skyler, now fully aware of Walt's criminal
enterprise, hatches a plan to safely launder

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:18.980
their money through the car wash that Walt
once worked at.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:24.720
Meanwhile, Jesse's moving on the drug dealers,
first by asking Walt to prepare ricin poison,

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:28.960
then by threatening to kill them any way that
he can, with or without Walt's help.

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:33.900
His plan is interrupted by Gus Fring, who's
known about Jesse's plan the entire time.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:38.680
The three of them have a meeting, where Gus
tells the drug dealers to stop using children.

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:43.959
In response, they kill Andrea's brother, and
Jesse responds by driving up with a gun of

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.560
his own to enact revenge.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:50.820
He's saved by Walt, who kills the dealers,
putting his own relationship with Gus at risk.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:55.540
Jesse goes into hiding, while Walt begins
to suspect that Gale is operating under orders

00:09:55.550 --> 00:10:01.079
from Gus to fully replicate Walt's meth formula,
so the kingpin can get rid of Walt for good.

00:10:01.079 --> 00:10:07.120
With the help of Saul, Walt lays a trap for
Gus, giving Jesse enough time to kill Gale,

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:11.490
ensuring that the drug lord won't be able
to kill them without crippling his meth operation.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:17.140
Their plan more or less works, but Gus responds
by isolating himself entirely from Walt and

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:17.640
Jesse.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.760
"Walter, you're never going to see him again."

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:24.520
Instead, all communication will be handled
by his "fixer," Mike Ehrmantraut.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.380
As a result, both Walt and Jesse begin spiraling
into darkness.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:33.840
Walt decides to buy a gun in case he needs
to kill Gus before Gus kills him, and while

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:38.240
dealing with serious guilt over killing Gale,
Jesse starts throwing money to the wind.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:44.520
Jesse's unhinged, depressed behavior is bad
news for Mike and Gus, so Mike begins taking

00:10:44.529 --> 00:10:48.519
the young chemist on some of his errand runs
in an attempt to provide a bit more purpose

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:49.540
to Jesse's life.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:52.260
Jesse's not the only one acting erratic, though.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:57.500
When Gale's body is discovered, law enforcement
assumes that he's Heisenberg, and that nearly

00:10:57.509 --> 00:11:02.600
throws Hank off the trail, until Walt's ego
gets in the way, and he convinces his brother-in-law

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:05.230
that Gale wasn't such a genius after all.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:12.860
"All his brilliance looks like nothing more
than just simple rote copying."

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:19.500
Still worried about Gus' vengeance, Walt convinces
Jesse to kill Gus with ricin hidden in a cigarette,

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.320
but Jesse misses his opportunity.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:26.790
However, Gus has other fish to fry besides
Walt, as a meeting with the cartel involves

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:32.449
completing a decades-long vendetta after Hector
Salamanca killed Gus' business partner years

00:11:32.449 --> 00:11:32.940
earlier.

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:38.740
The cartel is soon destroyed in an epic massacre,
and with Jesse's usefulness proven on the

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:42.500
trip, Gus asks him to take over the lab in
Walt's stead.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:45.840
Gus then tells Walt two pieces of very bad
news.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:50.620
First, Walt's out, with the understanding
that the only reason he's even alive is due

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:51.720
to Jesse's intervention.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:57.380
Second, Gus is going to kill Hank for investigating
him, with worse consequences for Walt and

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:58.899
his family if anyone interferes.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:03.779
Andrea's son, Brock, ends up in the hospital
with a flu-like illness, and when Jesse finds

00:12:03.779 --> 00:12:08.839
that the ricin hidden in his cigarette is
gone, he blames Walt, thinking that he poisoned

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:09.420
the child.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:14.640
Walt convinces him that it was Gus, and the
two agree to kill the drug lord, ultimately

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:18.500
succeeding with the help of Hector Salamanca
and his explosive wheelchair.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:31.300
Gus is dead, the underground laboratory is
destroyed, and Walt and Jesse both managed

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:31.900
to survive.

00:12:32.309 --> 00:12:37.160
However, Gus kept a laptop with security footage
of the lab, and with Gus' death, it's been

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.720
confiscated by the police.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:43.639
Walt teams up with Jesse and a reluctant Mike,
now healed from his cartel shootout, to wipe

00:12:43.639 --> 00:12:46.509
the laptop and keep them all out of jail.

00:12:46.509 --> 00:12:51.009
The plan goes smoothly, but their use of a
giant magnet accidentally reveals some of

00:12:51.009 --> 00:12:55.980
Gus' hidden bank accounts, giving the police
a fresh lead on Fring's secret meth empire.

00:12:56.309 --> 00:13:01.360
It's also revealed that Walt really did poison
Brock in order to turn Jesse against Gus,

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:04.960
and that Walt has no intention of stopping
his criminal activities.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:08.580
"You never told me that kid would wind up
in the hospital!"

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:12.320
"We're done when I say we're done."

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:17.560
With Gus out of the way, Walt sees the potential
for a replacement in the criminal underworld.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:22.980
Gus ran a massive organization with multi-state
distribution, and Walt believes that he, Jesse,

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:25.320
and Mike are just the men who can fill his
shoes.

00:13:25.689 --> 00:13:30.500
With the help of Lydia Rodarte-Quayle, an
executive at Madrigal, an international conglomerate

00:13:30.509 --> 00:13:35.139
with ties to Gus' old organization, the three
men plan to take over the distribution of

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:35.700
Gus' empire.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:41.300
With Lydia, Mike, and Saul's help, Walt and
Jesse start a new operation, moving their

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:45.180
meth lab from house to house under the guise
of a pest removal company.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:49.700
However, even though Walt is now the boss
of a huge business, that comes with assorted

00:13:49.709 --> 00:13:55.050
costs, like payouts to the pest removal company,
to his partners, and to Gus' former men serving

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:57.280
prison sentences in order to keep their silence.

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:01.420
Meanwhile, Walt's success in business comes
with a failure in his personal life.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:06.660
Skyler is becoming increasingly depressed
and horrified by Walt, and Walt's own separation

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:10.840
between his "Heisenberg" identity and his
day-to-day life is becoming blurred.

00:14:11.209 --> 00:14:15.920
When the DEA begins tracking one of the key
ingredients for their meth business at Madrigal,

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:21.160
Lydia offers them an alternative, a daring
train robbery that, if executed properly,

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:23.940
will mean enough methylamine for plenty of
cooks.

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:28.880
In order to make the operation go smoothly,
Walt and Jesse bring in Todd, one of the pest

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:29.860
removal employees.

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:34.759
The robbery seems to go smoothly, but it ends
in tragedy when the trio notice a young boy

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:37.080
watching them as they celebrate the desert
heist.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:41.880
Todd immediately shoots the kid, which forces
the crew to dispose of the body in a barrel

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.340
full of hydrochloric acid.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:49.060
Although the team manages to get away with
all the methylamine they could need, the boy's

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:51.080
death weighs heavily on Jesse.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:56.360
When Mike tries to buy out of the business
on the basis that the increased DEA surveillance

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:59.020
is too much for him, Jesse tries to leave,
too.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:03.840
However, Mike's buyer for his share of the
methylamine will only accept all or none of

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:08.540
it, since the offer is contingent on getting
rid of the blue meth that Walt makes.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:14.500
Walt refuses to give up on his criminal empire
since, with Skyler becoming increasingly horrified

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:18.260
by him, he has nothing left but his money
and his criminal reputation.

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:23.680
Walt eventually manages to convince the buyer
to take over as distributor for his meth,

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:26.300
while buying out Mike's share of the methylamine.

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:31.840
Mike agrees to continue paying for Gus' imprisoned
men out of his own share, but his plan is

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:35.180
stymied when the DEA catch his lawyer making
the money drops.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:41.079
Mike is forced to flee town, but Walt refuses
to let him leave unless he gives up the names

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:44.880
of Gus' men so Walt can silence them before
they have the chance to talk.

00:15:45.149 --> 00:15:50.439
The two men argue, and Walt shoots Mike to
death before remembering that Lydia also has

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.180
access to that information.

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:57.980
With the help of Todd's uncle, who runs a
crew of neo-Nazis, Walt has Gus' men killed

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:01.400
before Hank can get them to give up any information
on Heisenberg.

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:07.120
With his business safe, and Todd proving to
be an adept lab assistant, Walt rakes in the

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:09.620
cash for months before finally retiring.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:15.740
That is, until Hank finds a book given to
Walt by Gale on the toilet, and finally connects

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:16.600
all the pieces.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:21.320
Even though Walt is retired with plenty of
money, Hank is on his trail.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:26.860
Just before leaving town to start a new life,
Jesse realizes that Walt was actually behind

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:31.340
Brock's poisoning, which sends him on a crusade
against his former partner.

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:36.879
Hank picks Jesse up before he can burn down
the White household, and the two join forces

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.960
to gather evidence to take out Walt.

00:16:39.189 --> 00:16:44.959
Together, they trick Walt into revealing where
he stashed his drug money, and, desperate,

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:47.560
Walt calls his former neo-Nazi partners for
help.

00:16:47.889 --> 00:16:51.700
The neo-Nazis arrive, kill Hank, and kidnap
Jesse.

00:16:51.709 --> 00:16:56.259
Walt goes into hiding in New Hampshire, but
after seeing Elliott and Gretchen Schwartz

00:16:56.259 --> 00:17:01.279
on TV denying his involvement in the company
he co-founded, he comes back to tie up his

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:02.160
loose ends.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:06.580
He forces Elliott and Gretchen to launder
the rest of his drug money for his family,

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:10.740
and he admits to Skyler that everything he
did was for selfish reasons.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:19.160
"If I have to hear one more time that you
did this for the family-"

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.380
"I did it for me."

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:25.970
He then heads to the neo-Nazi compound, kills
the skinheads, and ultimately saves Jesse's

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:26.940
life in the process.

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:33.180
Dying of blood loss from a stray bullet, Walt
collapses in the neo-Nazis' meth lab, surrounded

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:35.240
by chemical equipment as the police arrive.

